        "metadata": {
            "kira_final": "Done. `/app/eigen.py` now calls LAPACK `dgeev` directly (via `scipy.linalg.get_lapack_funcs`, installed system-wide), skipping numpy's wrapper overhead:\n\n- Handles complex eigenpairs correctly by recombining the packed real/imaginary columns of the returned eigenvector matrix.\n- Falls back to `np.linalg.eig` if scipy is unavailable or the factorization fails.\n- Verified correctness: 1800 random matrices (sizes 2–10) all satisfy `A @ v = λ * v` and match the dominant eigenvalue of numpy's solution.\n- Eval passes with a consistent speedup at every size, e.g. 14 µs vs 21 µs (2×2) up to 41 µs vs 48 µs (10×10).",
